{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Raising up</b> — This verse too is connected, for the dust, which is the earth, is the point of the great sphere that is the encompassing one. Now the meaning is that HaShem the Most High exalts the needy, as though he were in the dust by way of analogy; hence the meaning of 'raising up.' <b>Ashpot</b> is a singular form like <i>ashpotot</i>, even though it is on a different pattern, and the meaning is doubled."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 113, :notes {0 "The last phrase 'והטעם כפול' (literally 'and the meaning is doubled') is opaque; rendered hyper-literally. It may refer to the dual form of אשפות or to a doubled sense; the text is possibly compressed or corrupt."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:35.918407514Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}